NEARS-1659 — task bug: 'N Reviews' summary pill wraps to two lines (mobile, English)
Screen: store reviews (Eco Market, store 19), emulator-5556 448x997dp, light, LTR.
Measured from ac9-reviews-ltr-loaded.png (3 px/dp):
  both pills (Expanded, equal flex): 65.7 dp wide -> inner width 55.7 dp
    (65.7 - 2 x Dimensions.paddingSizeExtraSmall = 5.0)
  '5 Ratings' ink width 50.0 dp, text block 10.3 dp tall  -> ONE line
  '5 Reviews' text block 21.7 dp tall                     -> TWO lines
  => sibling pills render at different heights (mint 60px vs outlined 90px device px)
Mechanism (this diff, total_rating_review_view_widget.dart):
  robotoMedium @ Dimensions.fontSizeExtraSmall (10.0, w500, letterSpacing 0)
  -> NearsText.labelSm (11px, w600, letterSpacing 0.22)
  All three changes increase advance width; '5 Reviews' sits ~0.5-1 dp over the fit.
NOTE: no RenderFlex overflow and no clipping (0 overflow lines in the whole session log);
the string is fully readable, so this does not literally break AC1/AC7's 'nothing clips'.
CAVEAT: base commit 7e0c44ee was NOT built on device, so the base one-line render is
inferred from the monotonic width increase, not directly observed.
